From ed61e3ab07937338cdb1791de003c609e30d3e5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JimmyBlunt <jo@paso-music.de>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:23:55 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] Run FastLED Patterns in a Web Worker with a watchdog
 (local #9002)

A loop() that never calls delay()/millis()/FastLED.show() (while (true) {})
froze the tab: main-thread wasm cannot be interrupted. The preview now runs
the sketch in a dedicated worker (fastled.worker.ts -> fastledWorkerCore.ts)
behind FastLedWorkerHost, which implements FastLedHostLike, so the handle,
render loop, packed frame and Art-Net output are unchanged.

- Same host calls in the same order, so bytes are identical; frames are
  pipelined by one IDE frame (frame(dt_k) requests frame k, shows k-1).
  A late answer repeats the last frame and accumulates the deltas.
- Watchdog: no answer within 2 s (setup: 10 s) -> worker terminated,
  friendly runtime error, last frame kept. Crashes reported the same way.
- ?fastledWorker=0 or no Worker keeps the main-thread host.
- Measured (Node worker_threads, 4,593 LEDs, 60 fps pacing, 600 frames):
  worker frame 0.86-1.03 ms, round trip 1.3-1.5 ms mean (max 6.6), 0
  repeated frames; main-thread cost per IDE frame 0.1 ms (was ~1 ms).
  Added latency = one IDE frame (16.7 ms at 60 fps).
- Tests: protocol/pipelining/watchdog with a fake port; golden L1/L2 through
  the worker path (0 differing bytes, one frame later); real threads:
  while(true) fixture terminated (multi-strip-blocked, both strips reported),
  show() runaway hits the budget and keeps running (Runaway.ino), rapid
  show() shows the last show (fork fixtures). Fixtures built by
  scripts/generate-fastled-fixtures.mjs --behaviour-only.

Pre-commit hook checks run manually (hook cannot spawn npx.cmd on Windows/Node 24):
eslint changed src files, check:e2e-coverage, check:e2e-locators, focused
tsc -p over changed files (clean; full tsc -b OOMs on this PC), vitest
fastledWorkerHost + fastledPatternHandle.wasm (21 passed). Browser: Blink
from the catalogue runs in the worker on 5175.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
